      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Tool-augmented LLM agents discover relevant APIs from large registries before planning execution, yet finite context windows prohibit injecting all tool definitions into a single prompt.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:24.208Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The dominant approach, which we term Retrieve-then-Plan (RtP), embeds the user query and retrieves similar tools via approximate nearest-neighbor search.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:24.208Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We study an alternative Plan-then-Retrieve (PtR) paradigm in which the LLM first generates Abstract Tool Stubs (hypothesized function signatures describing needed capabilities) which then serve as retrieval queries against the registry.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:24.208Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Evaluating on ToolBench (46,984 unique API endpoints, 50 categories) across single-tool (G1), intra-category multi-tool (G2), and cross-category multi-tool (G3) query subsets, we find a clear complexity-dependent crossover: RtP outperforms PtR on single-tool queries while PtR …",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:24.208Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This crossover holds at every retrieval budget (k=1 to 20), is robust across registry sizes from 1k to 47k APIs, and is consistent across model families (Gemini 2.5 Flash and gpt-oss-120b).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:24.208Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We further analyze token overhead and show that PtR’s extra discovery call roughly doubles inference cost, which pays off on multi-tool queries but hurts on single-tool ones, motivating complexity-adaptive routing as a practical direction—one that can be driven by a zero-cost …",
        "sourceUrl": "https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/plan-retrieve-tool-discovery",
        "source": "Apple Machine Learning Research",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z",
